      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+y^2&=\\frac{(t^2-1)^2+4t^2}{(t^2+1)^2}\\\\x^2+y^2&=\\frac{t^4+2t^2+1}{(t^2+1)^2}\\\\x^2+y^2&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x=1-\\dfrac{2}{1+t^2}<1$, the point $(1,0)$ is excluded.\nFor any other point on the circle, set $t=\\dfrac{y}{1-x}$. Using $y^2=1-x^2$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{t^2-1}{t^2+1}&=\\frac{y^2-(1-x)^2}{y^2+(1-x)^2}=x\\\\\\frac{2t}{t^2+1}&=\\frac{2y(1-x)}{y^2+(1-x)^2}=y\\end{align*}$$\nThus the curve is $x^2+y^2=1$, excluding only $(1,0)$.",
